# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefix-tiers development window (the preconverted GDN checkpoints and the host KV tier; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefix-tiers-1/<tag>/' *.env); every later job serves that one
# image. A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# T3 (SOFT): the TIMED RESTORE at ~32k, ~128k and ~254k (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-timed, scenario tier_timed) on the tier profile with its audit instruments off (the gate derives it: the `tiertime` kind, c2_prefix_gate.DERIVED; the digest check falls back to
# its sampled default). One cycle per size, smallest first: a cold prefill of the session (its TTFT), the next turn as a device-resident hit (the checkpoint restore alone: the P1b effect), floods the size of the pool so the session leaves the
# device, and the next turn again: the returning hit's TTFT is the tier's restore (the session's attention-KV pages written back from host RAM before vLLM looks for its hit, then the tail prefill) PLUS the spill of whatever the restored blocks displace
# from the full pool (those blocks are useful to their own tenants, so they are kept: a second device read of the same volume). The cold twin runs after it (it must equal the restored answer) and is not timed.
# READ (a measurement beside its exactness read; the verdict needs the restore on record and the pairs IDENTICAL): per size one line 'tier-timed-<n>: prompt <L> tokens; cold prefill TTFT; device-resident hit TTFT; returning hit TTFT (Q); restore <blocks> blocks
# <GB> in <ms> (GB/s); displaced blocks spilled in the same request: <GB> in <ms>'. The restore is worth it when the returning TTFT is well under the cold prefill's at the same L; the rates are what to plan with against docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md's
# 128k/254k table. NO CI load while it runs (the TTFTs are timings); CI need not be paused otherwise. Unqualified. Duration (estimate): 90 minutes plus the boot. Soft.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tier-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
